  m_text: A goalkeeper committing a foul in their own penalty area uses No booking/Yellow
    leniency checks, even for a challenge from behind or a professional foul, to
    avoid double jeopardy. A second yellow still sends the keeper off. Outside their
    own penalty area, regular foul discipline applies; handling the ball outside
    the box retains its separate straight-red rule.
